# THE WOOD (THE MAZE), SLAB 2 — 32 rooms: the band widens, two more cores.
#
# The honest lattice gains a northern and a southern row (so the wood is 5 rows
# deep instead of 3), two more thresholds at its far corners, and two more
# cores behind them.
#
# THE CORE PATTERN (rewritten 2026-08-03, when the wood stopped lying — see the
# head of slab 1). These were rings of 8 whose four exits per room were dealt by
# fixed offsets around the ring, so that nothing ever paired with its opposite.
# They are mazes now: a spanning tree cut over a 3x3 grid of the core's rooms,
# every corridor two-way. The old spills onto the band are cut; each core is
# entered and left by its threshold, and by whatever falls through its floor.

!region wood

